1
00:00:00,012 --> 00:00:01,392
Hestia got the fire.

2
00:00:01,792 --> 00:00:06,252
She was the first child Cronus
swallowed, and the last to come back up.

3
00:00:07,312 --> 00:00:09,952
Poseidon and Apollo
both asked to marry her.

4
00:00:10,592 --> 00:00:14,532
She laid her hand on Zeus's head
and swore never to marry at all.

5
00:00:14,932 --> 00:00:19,512
So instead of a husband, Zeus gave her
a place: the middle of every house.

6
00:00:19,952 --> 00:00:24,512
The first offering at every
feast went to her, and the last.

7
00:00:25,572 --> 00:00:29,412
Greek cities kept a public
hearth, and when colonists sailed

8
00:00:29,412 --> 00:00:33,132
off to found a new city, they
carried its fire with them.
